-192`) — `sanitizeDispatchVoice` strips control / bidi / zero-width chars from voice, but the identical sanitization is NOT applied to `metadata.Summary.Outcome` (`mode_local.go:192`) or commit subjects (`mode_local.go:199`). `json.Encode` with `SetEscapeHTML(false)` preserves raw bidi overrides / null bytes verbatim. Extract as `sanitizePromptString` and run bullet text through it.\n\n6. **Dispatch TUI duplicates patterns from `search_tui.go`** (`dispatch_tui.go:52-58`, `dispatch_tui.go:109-136`) — status-model lifecycle, ctx/cancel, spinner.Model, View() card composition, inline-clear helper all re-implemented. At minimum, `renderedLineCount` + the ANSI clear sequence `\"\\x1b[1A\\x1b[2K\\r\"` should live in a shared helper.\n\n7. **`--repos` values not validated as `owner/repo` slugs** (`options.go:19-22`) — `normalizeScopeValues` trims + dedupes but allows arbitrary strings (`\"../../etc\"`, `\"a b c\"`, newlines). Require `^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$`.\n\n8. **`go loadRepos()` prefetch leaks work if user picks Local** (`dispatch_wizard.go:220-230`) — fires a `gh api --paginate user/repos` call before the user picks a mode. Discarded on Local. Wasteful against GitHub API rate limits. Gate the prefetch behind mode selection.\n\n9. **Non-401 cloud errors leak endpoint in user message** (`cloud.go:187-194`) — output is `\"POST /api/v1/dispatches/generate: unexpected status 500: \\\"body\\\"\"`. Diagnostic-grade noise. Log the method/path via `logging.Warn` and return a trimmed user-facing string (or use `SilentError` per CLAUDE.md).\n\n10. **`ReadCommitted` error silently swallowed with `continue`** (`mode_local.go:175-178`) — data-integrity signal worth at least `logging.Warn` with CheckpointID + err. Today user gets a smaller-than-expected dispatch with no indication that some checkpoints were dropped.\n\n## Suggestions (Consider)\n\n11. **`\"N month\"` is 30 days, not calendar months** (`flags.go:85-87`) — `\"2 months ago\"` = `60*24h`. Surprises users near month boundaries. Use `AddDate(0, -n, 0)` or drop month from the grammar.\n\n12. **`newDispatchProgram` takes `altScreen bool` but every caller passes `false`** (`dispatch_tui.go:52-58`) — dead parameter.\n\n13. **Sibling repo discovery walks symlinks implicitly** (`dispatch_wizard.go:400-438`) — `entry.IsDir()` reports true for symlinks pointing at directories; `os.Stat(.../.git)` follows symlinks. Low risk but use `os.Lstat` or document as intentional.\n\n14. **`resolveRepoFullName` requires origin with parseable GitHub URL** (`mode_local.go:293-307`) — fresh local init or non-GitHub remote (SourceHut, self-hosted Gitea) fails the whole dispatch. Consider falling back to directory name.\n\n15. **`dispatchTextGeneratorFactory` hardcodes Claude Code** (`generate.go:21-27`) — no way to use Cursor / OpenCode even though `TextGenerator` interface exists for all of them. Read preferred agent from settings or add `--agent` flag.\n\n16. **`newDispatchStatusModel` hard-codes card height 12 and `min(max(width-8, 44), 76)`** (`dispatch_tui.go:109-136`) — 40-col terminals clamp to 44 and overflow. Pass `ss.width` through and respect it.\n\n17. **Flag-hide panic pattern** (`dispatch.go:77-79`) — matches `login.go`/`trail_cmd.go` so consistency is fine, but `MarkHidden` can't realistically fail. Replace with `_ = cmd.Flags().MarkHidden(...)`.\n\n18. **No length cap on literal `--voice` string** (`voices.go:33-35`) — 10MB voice string would be embedded verbatim in every LLM prompt. Cap at ~1 KB.\n\n## Praise\n\n- **HTTPS enforcement**: `requireSecureDispatchURL = api.RequireSecureURL` with test-only seam (`mode_cloud.go:19`), dedicated `TestServerMode_RejectsPlainHTTPBaseURL` that explicitly doesn't stub the guard (`mode_cloud_test.go:380-398`), plus matching `--insecure-http-auth` test.\n- **Default-branch ancestry gate** (`mode_local.go:258-277`) with three complementary regression tests.\n- **`reachableCheckpointIDsInRange` git-shim test** (`mode_local_test.go:61