{"timestamp":"2026-04-24T07:56:53.831Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"call_MPiNRvZMTvTdw2kFa8DXxiqA","output":"Chunk ID: 0357f7\nWall time: 0.0000 seconds\nProcess exited with code 0\nOriginal token count: 4090\nOutput:\nTotal output lines: 95\n\n# Review 02\n\n> Status: pending-dev\n> Date: 2026-04-24\n> Reviewer: Code Review Agent\n> Verdict: REQUEST CHANGES\n\n## Scope\n\nReviewed branch `entire-dispatch-codex` against `main` (PR #1004).\n\n- 28 commits on branch, 34 files changed (+5417 / −2) after excluding `.entire/`.\n- New package `cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/` (cloud + local modes, prompt building, voice presets) plus `cli` layer (wizard, Bubble Tea loading TUI, Glamour render).\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/... -count=1` — pass.\n- Did not run `mise run lint` / `mise run check` (scope-limited review).\n\n**Previous review status.** `review-01.md` is for an unrelated branch (`feat/entire-review`), so no dispatch-specific prior file-based review exists. Several self-imposed rounds of cleanup are visible in the commit log (HTTPS guard, default-branch ancestry, `--all-branches` local scoping). Those are reflected in the current code and look solid.\n\n## High (Must Fix)\n\n1. **High: dispatch TUI ignores `ACCESSIBLE=1` — screen-reader users get an animated spinner and ANSI-painted markdown.**\n   [cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go:84-98](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go:84) routes to `runInteractiveDispatch` + `renderTerminalMarkdown` purely on `dispatchTerminalMode(outW)`; no `IsAccessibleMode()` check. The wizard does the right thing at [cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go:237](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go:237) via `NewAccessibleForm`, but the generation step that follows runs a Bubble Tea spinner ([cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:62-91](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:62)) and then hands the result to Glamour ([cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:93-108](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:93)). Compare `search_cmd.go:73` which explicitly short-circuits TUI when `IsAccessibleMode()` is true. Since CLAUDE.md lists accessibility as a project invariant (\"always use the accessibility helpers for any `huh` forms/prompts\" and \"test new interactive features with `ACCESSIBLE=1`\"), this is a direct violation of the bar.\n\n   Fix: in `runDispatchCommand`, treat `IsAccessibleMode()` the same as non-terminal — skip the TUI, skip Glamour, print `RenderMarkdown(result)` directly. Add a test mirroring `search_cmd_test.go` that sets `ACCESSIBLE=1` and asserts no escape sequences appear in stdout.\n\n2. **High: wizard `currentBranch` resolver is called on every keystroke in local mode, shelling out to `git` each time.**\n   [cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go:311-325](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go:311) wires both `DescriptionFunc`s to `state.resolve(currentBranch)`. `state.resolve` unconditionally invokes `currentBranch()` whenever the mode is local ([cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options.go:38-45](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options.go:38)), and `currentBranch` is `GetCurrentBranch(ctx)` → `exec.Command(\"git\", ...)`. huh re-runs `DescriptionFunc` on every state update (key 2nd arg is `&state`, but huh's implementation re-evaluates on repaint). That is up to two `git` execs per keystroke inside the \"Confirm\" step. This also means the wizard is broken on detached HEAD — `currentBranchName` returns `\"not on a branch (detached HEAD)\"` ([cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:315](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:315)) and the Resolved Options / Command notes both render as `Validation error: not on a branch (detached HEAD)` with no way to progress.\n\n   Fix: resolve the current branch *once* before the form runs, cache it in `dispatchWizardState`, and have `state.resolve` read the cached value. If the lookup fails (detached HEAD), surface a clean error up front instead of deferring it into a note that blocks the whole form.\n\n## Important (Should Fix)\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go:70](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go:70) — `--local` help text says \"local LLM tokens\", which is misleading.** Local mode still invokes the installed Claude Code CLI (`claudecode.NewClaudeCodeAgent()` at [cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/generate.go:22](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/generate.go:22)), which uses the user's Claude account tokens, not a local model. Reasonable user reading of \"local LLM tokens\" is \"runs offline / no network\". Suggest: `\"generate via the locally-installed agent CLI instead of the Entire server\"`.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:155-161](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:155) — implicit-current-branch shell out runs `git log --all` across the full range, then `reachableCheckpointIDsInRange` shell-outs again.** `findCommitSubjectByCheckpoint` is called inside the per-checkpoint loop at [mode_local.go:199](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:199) and each call shells out to `git log --all --grep=... --format=%s%x00`. For a repo with N checkpoints in the window, that's O(N) `git log` invocations, each traversing all refs. With a realistic 7-day window this is usually a handful, but on a monorepo with dozens of checkpoints per day it could blow up. Minimum: do a single `git log --grep='Entire-Checkpoint:' --format='%H%x00%s%x00%B' --since=... --all` and build a `map[checkpointID]subject` once. Test coverage does not exercise this hot path at realistic scale.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/generate.go:188-192](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/generate.go:188) — `escapeDispatchPrompt` only defends against two exact section-delimiter strings; no defense in depth on untrusted bullet text.** `sanitizeDispatchVoice` strips control chars / bidi / zero-width from voice, but the identical sanitization is NOT applied to bullet `Text` values coming from `metadata.Summary.Outcome` ([mode_local.go:192](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:192)) or git commit subjects ([mode_local.go:199](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:199)). `json.Encode` with `SetEscapeHTML(false)` preserves raw bidi overrides and zero-width chars verbatim inside bullet strings. A crafted commit subject or `Summary.Outcome` containing `‮` or null bytes is passed to the LLM unsanitized. Not a critical injection (model will still read the JSON as structured data), but violates the principle the voice sanitizer establishes. Suggested: run bullet `Text` through `sanitizeDispatchVoice` (renamed — or extracted as `sanitizePromptString`) before JSON-encoding into the prompt.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:52-58](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:52), [cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:109-136](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:109) — dispatch TUI duplicates patterns already in `search_tui.go`.** `newStatusStyles(w)` is shared (good), but the status-model lifecycle (ctx/cancel, spinner.Model, View() card composition, `clearDispatchInlineView` inline-clear helper) is a re-implementation of the same shape used for search. With `mise run dup` at threshold 50 flagged elsewhere in the codebase, this is worth consolidating before shipping. At minimum, `renderedLineCount` + the ANSI clear sequence (`\"\\x1b[1A\\x1b[2K\\r\"`) should live in a shared helper — every future TUI that wants an inline loading card will re-invent it. Not a merge blocker but a tech-debt flag.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options.go:19-22](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/options.go:19) — `--repos` values are not validated as `owner/repo` slugs.** `normalizeScopeValues` trims + dedupes but allows arbitrary strings (e.g., `\"../../etc\"`, `\"a b c\"`, empty-after-trim, entries containing newlines). The backend probably rejects, but an earlier local-side check is cheap insurance (and produces a better error message). Minimum: require each value to match `^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` or similar.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go:220-230](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go:220) — `go loadRepos()` prefetch leaks work if user picks Local mode.** The goroutine fires a `gh api --paginate user/repos` call (potentially expensive, network-bound) before the user chooses a mode. If they pick Local, the response is discarded. Fine in terms of correctness (due to `sync.Once`), but wasteful against GitHub API rate limits and user-visible network activity. Gate the prefetch behind a cheap early-exit when the user's first…90 tokens truncated…nostic-grade noise for a CLI user; it also leaks the endpoint path into user-facing error text. Suggested: keep the method/path in a `logging.Warn`, and return a trimmed `\"dispatch service returned <status>: <body>\"` to the user, or use `SilentError` with a pre-printed user-friendly line (matches the error-handling pattern documented in CLAUDE.md § \"When to use `SilentError`\"). Note: 401 is handled well already ([cloud.go:184-186](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/cloud.go:184)).\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:175-178](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:175) — `ReadCommitted` error is silently swallowed with `continue`.** A failing `ReadCommitted` for a checkpoint that `ListCommitted` already surfaced is a data-integrity signal worth at least a `logging.Warn` (CheckpointID, err). Today the user gets a smaller-than-expected dispatch with no indication that some checkpoints were dropped.\n\n## Suggestions (Consider)\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/flags.go:85-87](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/flags.go:85) — `\"N month\"` is 30 days, not calendar months.** Minor, but `\"2 months ago\"` calculated as `60*24h` will surprise users near month boundaries. Either parse month arithmetic properly (`AddDate(0, -n, 0)`) or drop month from the grammar to avoid the footgun.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:52-58](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:52) — `newDispatchProgram` takes `altScreen bool` but every caller passes `false`.** Dead parameter. Remove or wire it to `tea.WithAltScreen()` for a future opt-in.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go:400-438](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_wizard.go:400) — sibling repo discovery walks symlinks implicitly.** `os.ReadDir(parent)` returns symlinked directory entries, `entry.IsDir()` reports `true` for symlinks pointing at directories, and `os.Stat(.../.git)` follows symlinks. Low risk (attacker needs write access to the parent directory), but if you want to be principled, use `os.Lstat` to reject symlinks, or document that this is intentional best-effort.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:293-307](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:293) — `resolveRepoFullName` requires an `origin` remote with a parseable GitHub URL.** A repo with no origin (fresh local init) or a non-GitHub remote (SourceHut, self-hosted Gitea) fails the whole dispatch with `\"find origin remote: ...\"`. Consider graceful degradation: use the repo's directory name as a fallback when the origin URL doesn't parse.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/generate.go:21-27](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/generate.go:21) — `dispatchTextGeneratorFactory` hardcodes Claude Code.** No way to use, say, Cursor or OpenCode as the local generator, even though the `TextGenerator` interface exists for all of them. Consider reading the preferred agent from settings (`GetAgentsWithHooksInstalled` intersected with `AsTextGenerator` capability) or from a `--agent` flag. Not blocking; a follow-up.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:109-136](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch_tui.go:109) — `newDispatchStatusModel` hard-codes card height to 12 and uses `min(max(width-8, 44), 76)`.** Small terminal windows (e.g. 40 cols) clamp to 44 cols and will overflow visually. Already have `ss.width` available via `newStatusStyles`; pass through and respect it.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go:77-79](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch.go:77) — `panic(\"hide insecure-http-auth flag: %v\", err)`.** This is the `login.go`/`trail_cmd.go` pattern, so consistency is fine. But a panic here can't realistically fire (cobra's `MarkHidden` only errors on unknown flag name). Consider replacing with `_ = cmd.Flags().MarkHidden(\"insecure-http-auth\")` and a comment — panics from command setup at import time are surprising.\n\n- **[cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/voices.go:33-35](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/voices.go:33) — literal voice string passthrough has no length limit.** A 10MB user-supplied `--voice` string is embedded verbatim in every LLM prompt. A cap (say, 1 KB) on literal voice text would prevent accidental foot-guns and reduce token usage on malformed input.\n\n## Praise\n\n- **Excellent HTTPS enforcement story on the cloud path.** `requireSecureDispatchURL = api.RequireSecureURL` with a test-only seam ([mode_cloud.go:19](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_cloud.go:19)), the dedicated `TestServerMode_RejectsPlainHTTPBaseURL` that explicitly does NOT stub the guard ([mode_cloud_test.go:380-398](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_cloud_test.go:380)), and the matching `--insecure-http-auth` test ([mode_cloud_test.go:328-373](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_cloud_test.go:328)). This pin-before-it-regresses pattern is the right shape for security-critical checks.\n\n- **Default-branch ancestry gate is both correct and well-tested.** `defaultBranchRef` requires the candidate to be an ancestor of HEAD ([mode_local.go:258-277](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local.go:258)), with three complementary regression tests: `TestDefaultBranchRef_RejectsStaleRefNotAncestorOfHEAD`, `TestDefaultBranchRef_RejectsStaleOriginHEADNotAncestorOfHEAD`, `TestDefaultBranchRef_AcceptsAncestor`. The commit history suggests this was discovered mid-development — the tests are the right response to that discovery.\n\n- **`reachableCheckpointIDsInRange` test uses a git shim script to assert that only `git log` invocations are captured, with an explicit comment explaining why.** [mode_local_test.go:616-662](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/mode_local_test.go:616). This is the kind of test that pays for itself when a future refactor reorders the resolution calls.\n\n- **Forward-compat JSON decoding on cloud responses.** `TestCloudClient_CreateDispatch_IgnoresUnknownResponseFields` ([cloud_test.go:170-194](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/cloud_test.go:170)) pins that unknown response fields do not break the client. Matching `APIBranches.UnmarshalJSON` accepting both `[\"x\",\"y\"]` and `\"all\"` sentinel is a clean forward-compat shape.\n\n- **Voice sanitization is thorough where it's applied.** Control chars 0x00-0x08, 0x0B, 0x0C, 0x0E-0x1F, 0x7F, zero-width (0x200B-0x200F, 0x2060-0x2069), and bidi overrides (0x202A-0x202E) all stripped; CR normalized to LF; trimmed. Tests cover null, bidi, and zero-width ([generate_test.go:65-78](cmd/entire/cli/dispatch/generate_test.go:65)). This is the right sanitizer; extending it to bullet text (see Important above) would close the circle.\n\n- **Clean mode separation between cloud and local with a small, explicit `Options` shape.** No shared global state beyond the test-only `lookupCurrentToken` and `nowUTC` hooks. Cloud-only and local-only concerns never cross-import.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe feature is large (5.4k LOC) but the code is structured sensibly, and the multi-round cleanup visible in the commit log has paid off — the security-critical paths (HTTPS enforcement, token usage, default-branch ancestry) are well-tested with regression pins that document why they exist.\n\nThe two High findings are both about accessibility / UX correctness on the happy path: screen-reader users get a broken TUI, and the wizard over-shells to git in a way that breaks on detached HEAD. Both are fixable in well under a day.\n\nThe Important findings are mostly tech-debt flags and defense-in-depth: the per-checkpoint `git log` fan-out, extending voice-style sanitization to bullet text, and the `--local` help string.\n\nNo evidence of token leakage in logs (searched for `logging.*` and `fmt.Print*` under dispatch — none touch the token). The `--insecure-http-auth` pattern matches `login`/`trail` exactly. No `SilentError` usage in dispatch, but the existing error strings are already user-readable; only the 5xx-path f